# wheel-ride.xrs - the power wheel rides the HUD window (VR-117, second headset
# report): a weapon switch by mouse scroll and the grip-hold loadout both open
# DisGFxMoviePlayerPowerWheel, and on the mono screen every switch dropped the
# world flat for a second. The pad maps a held LEFT grip to the wheel
# (pad_bridge: gripL > 0.9 -> LEFT_SHOULDER), so the sim squeezes it.
#
# Needs GAMEPLAY and the game window reachable. Log lines beside it:
# `ui/surface: context=Wheel ... rides=1`, `ui/ride: Wheel -> RIDING`.
#
#   tools\xrsim-run.ps1 -Path tools\xrsim\wheel-ride.xrs -Dir D:\dvr-data\xrsim
reset
# The aim dot (VR-57) is a quad layer too: park it so quadLayers counts the HUD alone.
@mod stereo reentry; hud on; hud menu on; crosshair dot off
@frames 240
@assert sessionState eq FOCUSED
@assert projectionViews eq 2
@assert quadLayers ge 1

# Hold the wheel open: the projection must STAY and the wheel ride the window.
grip l 1.0
@frames 150
@assert projectionViews eq 2
@assert quadLayers ge 1
@shot wheel_riding

# Release: back to gameplay with both eyes fresh, no drop to the screen.
grip l 0.0
@frames 120
@assert projectionViews eq 2
@assert eyeAgeL le 0
@assert eyeAgeR le 0
@shot wheel_released

# The A/B: with the wheel's opt-in off, the same hold takes the mono screen.
@mod hud menu Wheel off
@frames 30
grip l 1.0
@frames 150
@assert projectionViews eq 0
@shot wheel_screen
grip l 0.0
@frames 120
@assert projectionViews eq 2
@mod hud menu Wheel on; crosshair dot on
